          "text": "The pattern indexes as the **orthorhombic TiNiSi-type structure**, space group **Pnma (No. 62)**, with:\n\n- \\(a \\approx 6.981\\) \u00c5\n- \\(b \\approx 4.267\\) \u00c5\n- \\(c \\approx 7.358\\) \u00c5\n- \\(V \\approx 219.18\\) \u00c5\u00b3\n\nCe and Dy statistically share the rare-earth 4c site in the average powder structure. No strong unindexed reflections require an ordered Ce/Dy superstructure.\n\n```cif\ndata_CeDyNi2Ge2\n_audit_creation_method\n'Indexed and structure-matched from Cu Kalpha1 powder diffraction data'\n\n_chemical_name_common\n'CeDyNi2Ge2, TiNiSi-type average structure'\n_chemical_formula_structural        'CeDyNi2Ge2'\n_chemical_formula_sum               'Ce2 Dy2 Ge4 Ni4'\n_cell_formula_units_Z               2\n\n_symmetry_cell_setting              orthorhombic\n_symmetry_space_group_name_H-M      'P n m a'\n_symmetry_Int_Tables_number         62\n_space_group_name_H-M_alt           'P n m a'\n_space_group_IT_number              62\n\n_cell_length_a                      6.981\n_cell_length_b                      4.267\n_cell_length_c                      7.358\n_cell_angle_alpha                   90\n_cell_angle_beta                    90\n_cell_angle_gamma                   90\n_cell_volume                        219.18\n\n_diffrn_radiation_type              'Cu Kalpha1'\n_diffrn_radiation_wavelength        1.5406\n\n# Ce and Dy share one crystallographic rare-earth site.\n# Coordinates are refined/prototype-constrained estimates for the\n# TiNiSi-type RNiGe framework.\n\nloop_\n_atom_site_label\n_atom_site_type_symbol\n_atom_site_symmetry_multiplicity\n_atom_site_Wyckoff_symbol\n_atom_site_fract_x\n_atom_site_fract_y\n_atom_site_fract_z\n_atom_site_occupancy\n_atom_site_U_iso_or_equiv\nCe_R   Ce   4   c   0.0203   0.2500   0.6842   0.5000   0.0063\nDy_R   Dy   4   c   0.0203   0.2500   0.6842   0.5000   0.0063\nNi1    Ni   4   c   0.1815   0.2500   0.0612   1.0000   0.0063\nGe1    Ge   4   c   0.2910   0.2500   0.3818   1.0000   0.0063\n```\n\nRepresentative indexing is:\n\n| \\(2\\theta_{\\rm obs}\\) | Reflection(s) |\n|---:|:---|\n| 17.49\u00b0 | 101 |\n| 24.10\u201324.18\u00b0 | 011, 002 |\n| 25.49\u00b0 | 200 |\n| 27.33\u00b0 | 111 |\n| 33.13\u00b0 | 210 |\n| 34.64\u00b0 | 112 |\n| 35.37\u201335.43\u00b0 | 211, 202 |\n| 38.89\u00b0 | 103 |\n| 40.63\u00b0 | 301 |\n| 42.34\u201342.48\u00b0 | 020, 013 |\n\nAn ordered Ce/Dy lower-symmetry model is not justified by the pattern; it would require superstructure reflections that are not evident here.",
